Subject: [PATCH] gbp_agent: drop eventlet monkey-patch for OpenStack 2026.1

neutron 2026.1 is designed to run un-patched on native threads, and
neutron's own OVS agent entry point -- the class GBPOpflexAgent subclasses
-- no longer monkey-patches at all. Monkey-patching it back re-introduces
green threads under an agent whose base class no longer expects them.

Upstream chose the other way. Through the 18.2.1 tag these lines read

    from neutron.common import eventlet_utils  # noqa
    eventlet_utils.monkey_patch()  # noqa

which aborted the agent at startup on 2026.1, because neutron deleted both
``neutron.common.eventlet_utils`` and the whole ``neutron/cmd/eventlet/``
package:

    ImportError: cannot import name 'eventlet_utils' from 'neutron.common'

Upstream fixed that ImportError in f986945 "Add Gazpacho Support" by
keeping the monkey-patch and calling eventlet directly instead. That
resolves the import but not the reason the call is wrong here, so we still
remove it -- the same two-statement deletion as before, restated against
the new context. This is a deliberate, single-hunk divergence from
upstream and the only functional difference between our build and the
combination upstream gates against.

Applied against the installed copy in the venv, because the opflex-agent
Dockerfile runs kolla_patch after `pip install /opflex-agent`.
Path uses the version-independent `python3` symlink created in
docker/openstack-base/Dockerfile.j2.

--- var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/opflexagent/gbp_agent.py
+++ var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/opflexagent/gbp_agent.py
@@ -15,11 +15,6 @@
 import sys
 import time
 
-# We need to ensure that the monkey-patch gets applied
-# before other packages that use eventlet get imported
-import eventlet
-eventlet.monkey_patch()
-
 from neutron.agent.common import ip_lib
 from neutron.agent.common import polling
 from neutron.agent import rpc as agent_rpc
